    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŏvem</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>num. adj. card</i>. [kindred to Sanscr.
			navan; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννέα</span>; Germ. neun;
			Engl. nine], <i>nine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">novem orbibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rep. 6, 17, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sermo in novem et libros et dies distributus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q.
					Fr. 3, 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milia passuum decem novem,</span>”
				<i>nineteen</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 1, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
